# Wind sweep flight: 13 m/s. above 12 m/s, where the drone must return or land at once. A SHORT flight (sitl/survey.waypoints) that tests only whether ArduPilot's wind estimate shows the limit is crossed, and how fast.
# Mission: sitl/survey.waypoints
# Bands are the drone's operating limits (0-<5, 5-<8, 8-12, >12 m/s). Each band is tested at its
# upper edge, the worst case still inside it. Speeds were fixed after the calm flight and before
# any windy one, so they are not chosen to suit the detectors.
# Use after sitl.parm:  --add-param-file=<repo>/sitl/sitl.parm --add-param-file=<repo>/sitl/wind/wind_13.parm
SIM_WIND_SPD    13
# gusts: SITL's turbulence, about its standard deviation in m/s (SIM_Aircraft::update_wind).
# 30 % of the mean speed: our assumption for rough terrain such as a plantation, the same for every flight
SIM_WIND_TURB   3.9
SIM_WIND_TC     5
# from the south: tailwind going north, headwind coming home, crosswind on the survey lines
SIM_WIND_DIR    180
# 1 = no height limit: full speed at every height (the default 0 weakens wind below 60 m, so 40 m would get less)
SIM_WIND_T      1
# A bigger pack than sitl.parm's 3300 mAh, so the long mission does not run the battery flat
# in strong wind (v3's battery rule learns the drain per flight, so the pack size does not bias it).
BATT_CAPACITY   10000
